.env
# `.env` alone matches that exact name and nothing else, so every SIBLING an
# editor or a shell leaves behind stayed committable: `.env.save` (vi),
# `.env.bak`, `.env.swp`, `.env.local`. A real one was sitting untracked in
# this repo on 2026-08-20 holding live Alpaca and Anthropic keys — one
# `git add -A` from being published. Ignore the whole family and re-include
# the one member that is meant to be tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
HALT
logs/
# NO TRAILING SLASH. `.venv/` matches a DIRECTORY only. A git worktree used a
# .venv SYMLINK pointing into this checkout; the slash meant git did not ignore
# it, so it was tracked, merged in PR #89, and `git pull` here then replaced
# this checkout's REAL venv with a symlink to itself — taking down all ten
# launchd jobs at once, since every one of them invokes `.venv/bin/python`.
# Bare `.venv` matches both a directory and a symlink. Do not re-add the slash.
.venv
# ALL runtime state stays local: ledger, lessons, judgments, heartbeat,
# trade counts, backtest trials
memory/
.pytest_cache/
dashboard.html
dashboard_data.json
.site/
journal.html
blog.html
publisher_data/
evidence/
backups/
.DS_Store

# Isolated worktrees for implementation work (superpowers:using-git-worktrees).
# The live bot runs FROM this checkout via launchd, so implementation happens in
# a worktree rather than here — divergence #7 was "production running code nobody
# had reviewed", and editing risk.py in place while a cycle fires is that exact
# shape.
.worktrees/
